% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/plan_cli.py` as the THE HARNESS-FACING CONTRACT. Runs with no GUI process and no server. argparse add_subparsers(dest=..., required=True) - required defaults to False, so without it the CLI with no verb parses successfully and does nothing - plus add_parser() and set_defaults(func=...) per verb, which keeps 13 verbs and their nested sub-verbs from becoming an if-ladder. 'show --json' RETURNS THE SAME SHAPE AS THE ARRANGE ROUTE, so a harness and the GUI cannot disagree about what the plan is. 'build' calls plan_mix_build so CLI and GUI produce an identical artifact. Every mutation takes --base-rev or --force and prints the new rev. 'transition get|set|clear' mirrors the transitions route FIELD-FOR-FIELD: --from --to [--technique --beats --showcase-move --effects --note --author] --base-rev, with the same null-means-leave-unchanged semantics. --AUTHOR IS EXPLICIT AND IS NOT INFERRED FROM actor=cli, because an LLM shelling out and a human typing the same command are both actor=cli and inferring would mislabel exactly the case the PRD cares about. 'bunch list|new|activate|deactivate|archive', where 'bunch new --activate' composes create-then-activate in one invocation and reports a conflicting bunch by name, because a bunch that is created and never activated constrains nothing. 'mark <wip|ready|archived>' WRITES lifecycle state while the separate 'status' verb READS staleness; deliberately different verbs. 'note' is TRACK-scoped; transition notes go through 'transition set --note'.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

THE HARNESS-FACING CONTRACT. Runs with no GUI process and no server. argparse add_subparsers(dest=..., required=True) - required defaults to False, so without it the CLI with no verb parses successfully and does nothing - plus add_parser() and set_defaults(func=...) per verb, which keeps 13 verbs and their nested sub-verbs from becoming an if-ladder. 'show --json' RETURNS THE SAME SHAPE AS THE ARRANGE ROUTE, so a harness and the GUI cannot disagree about what the plan is. 'build' calls plan_mix_build so CLI and GUI produce an identical artifact. Every mutation takes --base-rev or --force and prints the new rev. 'transition get|set|clear' mirrors the transitions route FIELD-FOR-FIELD: --from --to [--technique --beats --showcase-move --effects --note --author] --base-rev, with the same null-means-leave-unchanged semantics. --AUTHOR IS EXPLICIT AND IS NOT INFERRED FROM actor=cli, because an LLM shelling out and a human typing the same command are both actor=cli and inferring would mislabel exactly the case the PRD cares about. 'bunch list|new|activate|deactivate|archive', where 'bunch new --activate' composes create-then-activate in one invocation and reports a conflicting bunch by name, because a bunch that is created and never activated constrains nothing. 'mark <wip|ready|archived>' WRITES lifecycle state while the separate 'status' verb READS staleness; deliberately different verbs. 'note' is TRACK-scoped; transition notes go through 'transition set --note'.

% Output

- Primary output: `brain/plan_cli.py`.
- PDD context tags: backend, cli, agent-interface.
- Keep changes scoped to the primary output and the smallest necessary caller/test adaptations.

% Verification

- Run the focused tests that cover `brain/plan_cli.py` and every declared interface.
- Run `UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/claw-dj-uv-cache uv run python -m unittest discover -s tests` before accepting a repository-wide sync.
- For Python modules, also run `UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/claw-dj-uv-cache uv run python -m py_compile brain/plan_cli.py`.
- Verify revision-conflict, missing-file, malformed-input, and legacy-compatibility paths relevant to this module.
- Do not require a model, GitHub, Mixxx playback, or network access for deterministic tests.

